      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was actually thinking of something similar, but instead there would be a single patch that undoes changes for newer boards in order to make proto boards work.\n\nOnly problem is that it would probably need to be rebased occasionally. Changing a #define in ToT seemed easier than cherry-picking a patch and dealing with potential conflicts.\n\nI was also thinking that the user could just add EXTRA_CFLAGS\u003d-D\u0027IS_PROTO\u003d1\u0027 to the build command, but that didn\u0027t quite work because board/\u003cboard\u003e/config.h is processed before EXTRA_CFLAGS. I\u0027m not sure if we want to update Makefile.toolchain for this or if doing so would have some other impact, but it seems like a useful idea in general. \n\nMaybe we can introduce a CONFIG_OVERRIDE environment variable in BUILD_CPPFLAGS for this sort of thing so that the user easily can tweak certain options at build time (documented in the C\u0026F guide) and we\u0027d guard the config variable (IS_PROTO) with #ifndef.",
